// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Diagnosis from attempt 27 vs best attempt 11:
//   1. 22/49 examples have "tiny" spans (1 token, e.g. <<total>>) because
//      CloseSpanIfComplete fires immediately on the first parser-complete token
//      (single identifiers are valid arithmetic-expression completions).
//   2. 19/49 examples emit no <<>> at all — model is in <think> mode and never
//      naturally produces << within the 900-token budget, and Phase 4 of the
//      best attempt had forbidden literal `next == "<<"` instead of RenderedEndsWith.
//
// Fixes applied to the best-result attempt (11, 100% syntax):
//   A. Add Phase 2a: run exactly `minTokens` ConstrainedStep iterations WITHOUT
//      calling CloseSpanIfComplete, giving the expression room to grow beyond 1 token.
//   B. Add Phase 5a: same minimum-token warm-up for spans detected in Phase 4.
//   C. Add Phase 7a: same warm-up for forced-open spans.
//   D. Fix all << detection to use RenderedEndsWith (eliminate forbidden literal equality).
//   E. Guard freeLimit to be at least 1 when maxSteps > 0 (fixes edge-case
//      progress postcondition for maxSteps == 1).
//   F. Keep all CloseSpanWithinBudget safety nets from attempt 11.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 – parser_validity:
//   Phase 1 (UnconstrainedStep): insideConstrainedOut stays false until
//     RenderedEndsWith(generated,"<<") triggers EnterObservedConstrainedSpan,
//     which sets currentConstrainedOut := [] — valid by precondition.
//   Phase 2a (minimum constrained, no close): ConstrainedStep returns a
//     parser-valid token or EOS; AppendConstrainedToken postcondition guarantees
//     IsValidPrefix is preserved. EOS path breaks without appending.
//   Phase 2b (constrained+CloseSpanIfComplete): CloseSpanIfComplete either
//     closes (insideConstrainedOut := false, implication vacuous,
//     currentConstrainedOut := []) or is a no-op; ConstrainedStep +
//     AppendConstrainedToken preserves IsValidPrefix as in Phase 2a.
//   Phases 3, 6, 7c, 8 (CloseSpanWithinBudget): postcondition guarantees
//     the invariant holds on exit.
//   Phases 4, 5a, 5b, 7 (OpenConstrainedSpan+loops): analogous to 1, 2a, 2b.
//
// Invariant 2 – progress (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   Phase 1: each iteration increments steps by 1 and appends at most 1 token
//     (EOS: no append). EnterObservedConstrainedSpan costs +0 and leaves
//     generated unchanged. Bound preserved.
//   Phase 2a: ConstrainedStep costs +1 step; AppendConstrainedToken appends
//     exactly 1 token (EOS breaks before append). Net: +1 step, ≤+1 token. ✓
//   Phase 2b: same as Phase 2a; CloseSpanIfComplete costs +1 step and appends
//     ">>" (1 token) when closing. Net: +1 step, ≤+1 token. ✓
//   Phases 3/6/7c/8 (CloseSpanWithinBudget with budget B): postcondition states
//     |generatedOut| <= |generated_entry| + B; we add B to steps. ✓
//   Phase 7 entry: OpenConstrainedSpan appends "<<" (+1 token) and we add 1 to
//     steps immediately after. Net: +1 step, +1 token. ✓
//   Phases 5a, 5b, 7a, 7b: analogous to 2a and 2b. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

